.Nd the IMP72 systems programming language, reference manual
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This is the reference manual of IMP72, as implemented by version 0.10.0 of the
.Nm imp
compiler for 64-bit Unix systems.
The language is the one of the compiler written for the PDP-10 by Walt Bilofsky
at the Yale University Department of Computer Science (DECUS program 10-198),
based largely on previous work of E. T. Irons;
substantial contributions were made by Steven Weingart and Terry Lyons.
