.Pp
The original compiler was designed and implemented by Walt Bilofsky
at the Yale University Department of Computer Science, based largely
on previous work of
.Ar E .
.Ar T .
Irons, with substantial contributions by Steven Weingart and Terry Lyons.
.Sh "APPENDIX I. RUNTIME LIBRARY ROUTINES"
The IMP run-time library, file
.Li libimp.a ,
contains the routines that the code of a program calls
.Li "(PRINT and READ among them\&)"
and the routines below, which a program may call.
A program calls the
.Li C
library through
.Ic CCALL
(Section 2.4.1).
The arguments of an IMP routine are addresses, so that in a call with
.Ic CCALL
the address of a variable is its argument.
Names are case sensitive.
.Bl -tag -width 5n -compact
.It Li FINI(I\&)
closes all the files and returns the output and the input to the standard
files; exits from the program if
.Ar I
is 0 (Section 2.2.7).
.It Li IFIX(X\&)
the integer part of the
.Ic REAL
.Ar X ,
truncated toward zero.
A value beyond the range is the least integer.
.Pp
impargc(0): the number of arguments of the command line of the program.
.Pp
impargvp(0): the address of the array of pointers to the arguments.
.It Li IMPARGET(OUT,V,I\&)
stores element I of the array of pointers
.Ar V
(a
.Li "char *[\&]" )
in the word at the address
.Ic OUT .
.It Li IMPARGSET(V,I,P\&)
stores the pointer
.Ar P
as element I of the array
.Ar V .
.It Li "IMPSTDIN(0), IMPSTDOUT(0\&)"
the
.Li "FILE *"
of the standard input and the standard output of the
.Li C
library, to give to
.Li "fputs, fgets"
and the like with
.Ic CCALL .
.Pp
impcalli(CODE,AC): the routine that
.Li CALLI(CODE,AC\&)
calls (Section 2.2.9).
.Pp
impblk(A,B,N): the routine that
.Ic MOVE
calls: copies
.Li N+1
words from
.Ar B
to
.Ar A .
.Pp
impmain: the function that the statements before the first
.Ic SUBR
of a file make.
.El
.Pp
The other symbols of the library are lower case names that begin with
.Li imp
.Pf \&( Li "imppr, imprd, impxct, impibp, impldb, impdpb, implsh, impash, improt, impblt, impac, impca, impbpp, impbpv, impxw" )
or upper case names that begin with
.Li "RTL, SC"
or
.Li IMPCORE :
the compiler calls them for
.Ic PRINT ,
.Ic READ ,
byte pointers, shifts by a variable count,
.Ic EXECUTE
and the like, and the library uses them itself.
A program should not define a name of that kind.
